The composite effective tunability (~10%) is lower than the bulk BST tunability (~70%) due to dilution in the polymer matrix — as predicted by Maxwell-Garnett theory (see B1 and B8). Increasing BST volume fraction raises composite tunability but worsens dispersion stability above 30 wt%.

=== Resonant Frequency Tuning via BST Bias ===

The [[Psi Stabilizer]] resonant frequency <math>\omega_{010}</math> shifts with BST bias voltage through:

:<math>\omega_{010}(V) = \frac{k_{010}}{{\sqrt{\varepsilon_\psi(V)\,\mu_\psi}}}</math>

For a 10% change in <math>\varepsilon_\psi</math> (0V to 200V bias):

:<math>\frac{\Delta\omega_{010}}{\omega_{010}} \approx -\frac{1}{2}\frac{\Delta\varepsilon_\psi}{\varepsilon_\psi} \approx -5\%</math>

At 40 kHz target frequency: tuning range ≈ ±1 kHz. This is the frequency servo range available to the [[Anchor Controller]] (D6) for impedance matching via BST bias — sufficient to track operator HRV coherence state variations without mechanical reconfiguration.

